    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full `BUILD SUCCESS`. \n\nDone. Summary of the change:\n\n**What I added**\n- A new function class `AuditOwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 a single small step that emits the immutable structured event to the `AUDIT` logger:\n  `{\"seq\":N,\"ownerId\":\u2026,\"customerCode\":\"\u2026\",\"membershipLevel\":\u2026,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n  - `seq` is a monotonically increasing `AtomicLong` across creates.\n  - The primary identifier is read through a one-line private `identifier(Owner)` helper (returns `customerCode` today) \u2014 so when the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, only that single line changes and the event automatically carries the memberId.\n- One new pipeline step `auditEvent` in `owners.POST.yml`, wired between the existing `audit` line step and `respond`.\n\n**Structural impact**\n- The existing `AuditOwnerCreated` (and every other class) is untouched \u2014 no method grew, no large class was edited. The only changed function is the new class's `service` method, which sits in a class with near-zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other \u2248 0). Two files touched (new Java class + YAML wiring).\n\nBoth the pre-existing behaviour (the audit line) and the new structured event now emit, and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass).",
